  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The problem: using Lock All makes the head scrunch up when sitting down, like as though it's that stereotypical meme of being hunched over on the computer for hours. Using Lock to Hip makes it look accurate when sitting, but when you lay down your view point will drift a bit. If you use \"Lock to Head\" your viewpoint will always be at the same spot, but your hip will move further down than expected. The solution would be to have an in between of the two without the crunching and it would be to lock to the chest. It could be something experimental for IK2 but it would help a lot to make sure that the hips and the head are in accurate positions.",
